# Security hardening

Run this checklist before every production release and when adding API routes.

## API route audit

For every file in `app/api/**/route.ts`:

- [ ] Calls `auth()` and returns 401 if unauthenticated
- [ ] Enforces role/group authorization before reads or writes
- [ ] Validates input with zod (reject unknown fields)
- [ ] No sensitive data in error messages or logs
- [ ] Rate-limit expensive endpoints (translation, file upload)
- [ ] No open/public routes unless explicitly documented

## Secrets exposure

- [ ] No API keys, DB URLs, or `AUTH_SECRET` in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars
- [ ] `.env.local` and `.env` are gitignored
- [ ] Client bundles contain no `process.env` secrets (verify with `next build` output)
- [ ] Anthropic/OpenAI keys only in server route handlers or `services/`

## Middleware

- [ ] `middleware.ts` protects all pages except `/login`, auth callbacks, and static assets
- [ ] Review matcher regex — `api` excluded from middleware is intentional only for auth callbacks
- [ ] API routes enforce their own auth (middleware exclusion ≠ open API)

## CORS

- [ ] Default: no custom CORS headers (same-origin only)
- [ ] If cross-origin needed: explicit allowlist of origins, never `*`
- [ ] Preflight only on routes that require it

## Headers & config

`next.config.ts`:

```ts
const securityHeaders = [
  { key: "X-Frame-Options", value: "DENY" },
  { key: "X-Content-Type-Options", value: "nosniff" },
  { key: "Referrer-Policy", value: "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" },
  { key: "Permissions-Policy", value: "camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()" },
];
```

- [ ] `reactStrictMode: true`
- [ ] CSP configured for production (start restrictive, loosen as needed)
- [ ] `poweredByHeader: false`

## Caching

- [ ] User-specific or auth-gated responses: `Cache-Control: private, no-store`
- [ ] Static assets: rely on Next.js defaults
- [ ] Never cache authenticated API responses at CDN without `Vary: Cookie`

## Dependencies

- [ ] `npm audit` — no high/critical unmitigated vulnerabilities
- [ ] Pin major versions; review new deps against license rules
- [ ] No typosquat packages — verify npm package names and download counts

## Database

- [ ] Parameterized queries only (`sql\`...\`` tagged templates)
- [ ] Row-level authorization in SQL WHERE clauses (user_email, scope)
- [ ] Migrations reviewed — no accidental data exposure

## Entra / Auth.js

- [ ] Enterprise app: assignment required
- [ ] Redirect URIs match exactly (prod + localhost)
- [ ] `AUTH_SECRET` is 32+ random bytes
- [ ] Session strategy appropriate (JWT for serverless; validate expiry)
